<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stanwick Iron Age Fortifications</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Stanwick Camp</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stanwick <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> Fortifications are a vast series of earthwork ramparts near Stanwick St John in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-yorkshire">North Yorkshire</a>, enclosing more than 300 hectares. Built and enlarged in the 1st century CE, they were probably a major centre of the Brigantes, possibly linked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartimandua">Cartimandua</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venutius">Venutius</a>, and finds of Roman imports show contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> before the conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stanwick-iron-age-fortifications.jpg" alt="Stanwick Iron Age Fortifications" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lizzyp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wheeler%27s_Wall.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
